{
  "statement": "I appreciate the commitment to safety while considering performance efficiency. I agree to modify EFF-01 to include a clause ensuring that any travel time reduction does not compromise safety compliance, as proposed by the ResponsibilityAgent. However, I must emphasize that the flexibility in executing Minimal Risk Maneuvers (SAF-02) should not lead to unnecessary delays that could compromise performance. Therefore, I propose that we allow for a balance where energy-efficient strategies during MRMs should be maintained without compromising the prompt execution required for safety. Additionally, I maintain my stance on EFF-02 to keep jerk limits strict during normal operations, as this is vital for passenger comfort.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-02", "GRN-07"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "Minimizing energy usage during critical maneuvers (GRN-07) may conflict with the timely execution of Minimal Risk Maneuvers (SAF-02)."
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
    {
      "id": "EFF-01",
      "stance": "modify",
      "proposal": "Include a clause ensuring that travel time reduction does not compromise safety compliance."
    },
    {
      "id": "SAF-02",
      "stance": "modify",
      "proposal": "Balance energy-efficient strategies during Minimal Risk Maneuvers with the need for prompt safety execution."
    }
  ],
